  "raw_text": "Step 1: Determine the possible remainders when dividing by 4 and by 5.\n- When dividing by 4, the possible remainders are 1, 2, 3.\n- When dividing by 5, the possible remainders are 1, 2, 3, 4.\n\nStep 2: Identify the total number of outcomes.\n- There are 3 possible outcomes for the first spin (remainder when divided by 4).\n- There are 4 possible outcomes for the second spin (remainder when divided by 5).\n- Therefore, there are \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) total possible outcomes.\n\nStep 3: List all possible combinations of remainders and their corresponding squares on the checkerboard.\n- (1,1) -> (3,1)\n- (1,2) -> (3,2)\n- (1,3) -> (3,3)\n- (1,4) -> (3,4)\n- (2,1) -> (4,1)\n- (2,2) -> (4,2)\n- (2,3) -> (4,3)\n- (2,4) -> (4,4)\n- (3,1) -> (5,1)\n- (3,2) -> (5,2)\n- (3,3) -> (5,3)\n- (3,4) -> (5,4)\n\nStep 4: Identify which of these squares are shaded.\n- Shaded squares are at (3,1), (3,3), (4,2), (4,4), (5,1), (5,3).\n\nStep 5: Count the number of shaded squares.\n- There are 6 shaded squares.\n\nStep 6: Calculate the probability of landing on a shaded square.\n- Probability = Number of favorable outcomes / Total number of outcomes = \\( \\frac{6}{12} = \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}<|im_end|>",
